## Goal

When a counted game pays its result, the page loads the account's card proficiency again. That result is `match.economy` set on `/match/:id`, which ladder, unranked and Conquest games all use. The Collection then shows the level and plays the game earned, and the newly unlocked stamp can be worn at once, with no page reload.

- The handle that `startProficiencyAccountSync` returns gains `reload()`. It queues the existing `reload` behind any stamp pick already in flight.
- A new export, `reloadOwnProficiency()`, calls `reload()` on the shared sync. It does nothing when no sync runs (no active account).
- A new ruling, R4977000 (amends R3013001), records the change. Its §11 paragraph goes in `spec/pending/4977.md`, and §14.14 gets one sentence.

## Files to touch

| File | new/change | What |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `apps/web/src/cards/proficiencySync.ts` | change | header comment; `reload()` on type `ProficiencyAccountSync` and on the object `startProficiencyAccountSync` returns; new export `reloadOwnProficiency()` |
| `apps/web/src/routes/match.tsx` | change | import `reloadOwnProficiency`; call it in `MatchRoute`'s `paid` effect beside `announceWallet()` |
| `apps/web/src/cards/proficiencySync.test.ts` | change | move the `ready` helper to module scope; add three `R4977000 …` tests |
| `apps/web/src/routes/match.test.tsx` | change | imports; one `R4977000 …` test in `describe("the XP reveal on a finished match (#1664)")` |
| `spec/rulings/R4977000.md` | new | the ruling note |
| `spec/pending/4977.md` | new | its §11 paragraph |
| `spec/14-economy.md` | change | §14.14, end of the **Stamps.** paragraph (line 245): one sentence linking `[[R4977000]]` |
| `apps/web/README.md` | change | the Collection row's proficiency sentence (lines 869-871): loaded again by a paid result |

Do not touch:
- anything under `crates/`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/` or `.claude/`;
- `spec/11-rulings.md`, `spec/INDEX.md`, `spec/CARDS.md` or `spec/history/`;
- `spec/rulings/R3013001.md`: its text says nothing about when the client loads, so no sentence of it changes;
- `apps/web/src/economy/wallet.ts`: `announceWallet()` must not make the call, because practice, `DuosBoard.tsx` and `NewsPanel.tsx` announce through it and count no plays.

Add no patches fragment, since no card changes (#4857, the R4780000 precedent, had none). Do not run `cargo jackioh spec index`.

Governing: SPEC §14.14; R3013000 (the server counts plays in the result's transaction), R3013001 (stamps and the client's copy), R4780000 (the precedent: a paid result re-reads owned cosmetics).

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/cards/proficiencySync.ts`, header comment (lines 1-7).** In line 3, change "The sync loads it once an active account is on a gated screen, sends each stamp…" to "The sync loads it once an active account is on a gated screen, and again when a counted game's result pays the account (`reloadOwnProficiency`, R4977000), sends each stamp…". Rewrap only the lines that sentence spans and leave the rest of the comment as it is.

2. **Same file, type `ProficiencyAccountSync` (lines 26-31).** After `settled(): Promise<void>;` add:
   ```ts
   /** R4977000: load the account's copy again, after any request already queued (a stamp pick in flight). */
   reload(): void;
   ```

3. **Same file, the object `startProficiencyAccountSync` returns (lines 69-76).** After `settled,` add:
   ```ts
   reload: () => {
     if (!stopped) enqueue(reload);
   },
   ```
   The `reload` inside is the existing local `const reload`. `enqueue` is the same `requestQueue()` the picks use, so the reload waits behind a pick with no extra code.

4. **Same file, new export** between `useProficiencyAccountSync` (ends at line 129) and `resetProficiencySyncForTests`:
   ```ts
   /** R4977000: a counted game's result changed the account's plays and levels (R3013000): load its copy again. No sync running, no request. */
   export function reloadOwnProficiency(): void {
     shared?.sync.reload();
   }
   ```

5. **`apps/web/src/routes/match.tsx`.**
   - Add `import { reloadOwnProficiency } from "../cards/proficiencySync.ts";` on its own line, directly above `import { announceWallet } from "../economy/wallet.ts";` (line 26).
   - Replace the `paid` effect (lines 253-258) with:
   ```tsx
   // #1664: the result's write paid this account (the Jlore, and maybe a level's or a quest's), so the
   // pill reads the wallet again, once however many views carry the answer. R4977000: the same write counted the
   // seat's plays (R3013000), so the page loads the account's card proficiency again too.
   const paid = match.economy !== null;
   useEffect(() => {
     if (paid) {
       announceWallet();
       reloadOwnProficiency();
     }
   }, [paid]);
   ```

6. **`spec/rulings/R4977000.md`** (new), exactly:
   ```markdown
   ---
   id: R4977000
   title: "A counted game's paid result loads the account's card proficiency again, so a level the game earned and its stamp show and can be worn without a reload (issue #4977; amends R3013001)"
   cards: "§14.14, R3013000, R3013001, R4780000, issue #4977"
   proven_in:
     - apps/web/src/cards/proficiencySync.test.ts
     - apps/web/src/routes/match.test.tsx
   ---
   The server counts a seat's plays in the transaction that records the result of every ladder, unranked and Conquest game ([[R3013000]]), but the page loaded its copy of the account's proficiency ([[R3013001]]) once, when the shared sync started, and again only after a refused pick. The sync outlives the move from the match to the Collection, so a level a game reached still read as before, and its stamp could not be picked (`writeOwnStamp` refuses a stamp above the level the page holds), until a reload.

   A paid result on the match screen (`match.economy` set, once however many views carry it) calls `reloadOwnProficiency()`, beside `announceWallet()`. It queues a `GET /api/proficiency` on the shared sync, after any stamp pick already in flight, and the answer replaces the page's copy. With no sync running (no active account on a gated screen) it sends nothing.

   One more read per counted game, the read the page already makes on its first gated screen. Practice, the co-op board and the news panel's claims announce the wallet without counting a play and load nothing.

   The client decides no level and no unlock (CLAUDE.md rule 7): it shows what the account answers.

   Hearthstone semantics: a reward earned in a game is usable when the game ends ([[R4780000]]).

   Rejected: calling it from `announceWallet()`'s no-balance branch, as [[R4780000]] did, since practice, co-op and the news claims announce there and count no plays; a read on every route change; the result carrying the new levels (a wire change to save one read).
